', N'Internally process Sn/As liquor to eliminate costly hazardous waste disposal.', N'10114', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/8868.jpeg', N'Historically, the Sn/As solution (TUS Caustic Discharge) generated at the Precious Metals Refinery is being disposed of through a third party vendor, GFL, to a hazardous waste disposal facility in the US. The PMR was looking for alternatives to this method due to high disposal cost, lack of disposal vendors, and potential PM recovery value.
Processing the Sn/As solution on-site would be beneficial since the disposal fee would be removed and along with the risks of having a single disposal vendor. Also, the recovery of trace amounts of PMs through recycling to Sudbury would benefit overall PM recovery. Based on the service fees for the hazardous waste disposal vendor to ship Sn/As offsite, the savings could exceed $316,800 annually, which accounts for a significant portion of the PMR’s services budget. Additionally, reagent consumption in the Cu/Ni neutralization circuit would be inherently reduced significantly. ', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/8868.jpeg', N'The Sheridan Park research team proposed a treatment method that involves neutralizing the caustic Sn/As solution with another acidic by-product generated on site, TUS Leached Copper. This solution is the filtrate from the TUS acid leach and is currently processed by being bled into the CuNi precip circuit. The proposed alternative is to neutralize the Sn/As with the Leached Cu solution, precipitating all metals, based on a Sheridan Park bench test. This slurry could subsequently be introduced to the Cu/Ni precipitation circuit and shipped as Cu/Ni/SiO2 recycle shipments. 
Plant trials at the PMR have proved successful and fairly robust; all Arsenic (As), Selenium (Se) and metals in solution were fully precipitated in the initial neutralization reaction. Batches were blended and reverted to the Smelter with regular CuNiSiO2 shipments, rather than needing to utilize a contractor for hazardous waste disposal.', N'https://globalvale-my.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/personal/reed_bell_vale_com/IQAQtNEZp-hNSo_xi_v-IXDwARiodDjf46T3Yp7o9nGUWsY?e=Z3s0Oe', N'With a successful plant trial implementation, the PMR no longer needs or relies on costly hazardous waste disposal of Tin-Arsenic. Essentially all generated liquor can be internally recycled, treated and reverted, eliminating the need for disposal. ', N'Effective precipitation of hazardous Arsenic at the plant scale, precipitated Selenium was able to effectively settle in the thickeners, small particle Selenium & Arsenic was not observed in the Pond effluent', 310000, 3, N'Eliminação da contaminação da graxa: O suporte mantém o balde estável e bem posicionado, prevenindo derramamento de graxa no solo, diminuindo desperdícios e riscos ambientais.', '2025-12-19T00:00:00.000', '2026-03-23T14:41:20.000', N'81047094', NULL, NULL);
Essa situação pode impactar a continuidade das atividades, a segurança dos colaboradores e o cumprimento dos procedimentos de bloqueio e etiquetagem.', N'Garantir confortabilidade de controles das chaves ', N'10121', N'01 - Imagens/01 - Antes/8870.jpeg', N'A área não possuía um controle padronizado para as chaves e caixas de bloqueio. Cada operador armazenava os materiais de forma diferente, sem um local definido ou identificação clara dos dispositivos. ', N'01 - Imagens/02 - Depois/8870.jpeg', N'Para melhorar o controle das chaves e aumentar a segurança operacional na área, foi implementada uma solução organizada e padronizada no posto pesado. A ação consistiu na instalação de um armário exclusivo para armazenamento das caixas de bloqueio, acompanhado de cadeados devidamente etiquetados, contendo a identificação clara do dispositivo ou ponto onde cada bloqueio se aplica', NULL, N'Sim', N'Processo com mais fácil acesso.', 0, NULL, N'COM A IMPLANTAÇÃO EVITOU PARADAS EM CORRETIVAS E NÃO BRITAVEIS. ', '2026-03-19T00:00:00.000', '2026-03-23T15:23:13.000', N'81058450', NULL, NULL);
