The original problem identified inconsistent peer training, reliance on individual knowledge, lack of standardized references, and gaps in onboarding new or transitioning employees. The project goal was to standardize training and onboarding to improve consistency, reduce missed steps, and create a sustainable model.
Following implementation, these gaps were addressed through the introduction of a centralized peer training binder and area-specific onboarding checklists. Training is now delivered using standardized guidelines, expectations are clearly documented, and supervisors have a structured way to verify that employees are properly set up before working independently. As a result, variability between trainers was reduced, onboarding became more consistent and efficient, and the training process is now more sustainable and repeatable.', N'Standardizing training early and documenting critical processes is essential to reducing variability and dependency on individual knowledge. Providing clear, accessible reference materials and structured onboarding checklists improves consistency, accountability, and sustainability, while making it easier to support new employees, role changes, and workforce turnover without disrupting operations.', 0, NULL, N'Time saved from resampling due to unknown bottle contents.', '2026-04-30T00:00:00.000', '2026-05-01T23:06:03.000', N'81022150', NULL, NULL);
